p = "experiments/E320_soft-attach-replaces-snap/experiment.md"
s = open(p, encoding="utf-8").read()
a = s.index("**Rule.** **KEEP**")
b = s.index("**Kill criterion (not enforced during the run).**")
rule = '''**Rule (the lane lead's final form, 2026-11-13 00:25).** **KEEP** (the snap's end geometry is replaced inside the network, with the snap's wiring) when, on BOTH seeds, topo F1 of the PRIMARY read-out of a is at least u' + 0.005 (0.6756 / 0.6810; this implies a >= c - 0.01 = 0.6725 / 0.6764 on both seeds, because u' + 0.005 lies above c - 0.01) with the guards held (F1@1.0, dup_frac, vertices, junction F1 against c: junction F1 at least 0.2894 / 0.2843, which u' itself passes: 0.3055 / 0.2964; topo precision of u' equals c's). **TIE** (token of D82, kept: "partial: the attachment helps, it does not replace the snap") when a is in [u', u' + 0.005) on a seed, no seed below u'. **CUT** when a is below u' on either seed (the attachment makes the keypoint geometry worse) or a guard breaks. Notes written before the run: (1) **The window is narrow.** c - u' is 0.0119 / 0.0104 and the seeds differ by about 0.004; the bound u' + 0.005 is about half of the geometry share (0.0104 - 0.0119), set from the numbers of both seeds. KEEP says that the attachment closes about 42 % / 48 % of the geometry window on both seeds; inside the seed spread that is a statement about a trend on two seeds, not a measurement of a small effect. (2) The prediction (a - c = -0.006, i.e. a - u' = +0.0059 / +0.0044) sits at the KEEP bound: close to a coin flip near the bound, by the numbers alone. (3) **The secondary read-out cannot pass c - 0.01 and the rule does not read it:** under the proximity wiring the end geometry is worth only snap-all - u = +0.0089 / +0.0059, so its ceiling is about 0.653 / 0.654 (about 0.032 below c, `--snap --snap-all` of E312); this is a property of the wiring, stated here and not part of the verdict. (4) **Junction guard:** read against c as written for the PRIMARY (evaluable: the matched wiring passes it with the keypoints); for the secondary and the tight read-outs it is not evaluable under proximity wiring (see above). The snap's junction gain is wiring-driven too (E311 section 3 on E305 s0: snap-all +0.0221 against snap +0.0373 junction F1 over the plain graph). (5) `better` map: dup_frac and vert100_dp are lower-is-better, so `max_loss` there means "not more than 0.01 / 1.0 higher"; the verdict is by hand, the map makes `decide.py` read the guards right if it is ever run on these cards (its clauses are the KEEP clauses: the TIE / CUT split above is by hand). (6) **Attribution:** arm a carries the E317 geometry loss (`--geom-w 0.5`), c and u' do not; a KEEP or a TIE can therefore be the geometry loss alone (E317 predicts about +0.015 unsnapped from it; held by D85, not run). The missing reference is E317 arm g read out with the same primary wiring (the keypoint ends of a network trained with the geometry loss); the within-run comparison above (a's own keypoints against its attached ends, same wiring) and the E317 run, if it is released later, separate the two. (7) The point estimate decides; next to the verdict the PAIRED scene-bootstrap interval of (a - c) per seed is reported: `jdiag.py boot e320_a_s<S> ends_card_snap_nogeom_attach_thr0.1 e312_p_s<S> ends_card_snap_thr0.1` (1000 resamples of the VAL scenes; the per-frame counts are written by `score` next to the card; the interval is not part of the rule).

'''
s = s[:a] + rule + s[b:]
def rep(old, new):
    global s
    assert s.count(old) == 1, (old[:60], s.count(old))
    s = s.replace(old, new)
rep('''  {"metric": "topo_F1", "vs": "c", "max_loss": 0.01},
  {"metric": "topo_F1", "vs": "u", "min_effect": 0.005},''', '''  {"metric": "topo_F1", "vs": "u", "min_effect": 0.005},''')
rep('''the rule is rewritten (KEEP: a >= c - 0.01 and a > u' + 0.005; the clause "above u + 0.02" is dropped: unreachable by design once the wiring is held equal)''', '''the rule is rewritten to the lane lead's final form (KEEP: a >= u' + 0.005 on both seeds, which implies a >= c - 0.01; TIE: a in [u', u' + 0.005) on a seed; CUT: a below u' on either seed or a guard broken; the clause "above u + 0.02" is dropped: unreachable by design once the wiring is held equal)''')
rep('''The ceiling of the proximity wiring is E312 `--snap --snap-all` (0.6527 / 0.6540), not c;''', '''The ceiling of the proximity wiring is E312 `--snap --snap-all` (0.6527 / 0.6540, about 0.032 below c: under proximity wiring the end geometry is worth only +0.0089 / +0.0059 over u), so this read-out can never pass c - 0.01, a property of the wiring and not of the attachment;''')
open(p, "w", encoding="utf-8").write(s)
print("card3 ok")
